+# CareerOps upgrade — audit & change log (2026-10-23)
+
+Scope: GitHub snapshot `Job-Hunt-Command-Center-main.zip` (no `.git` directory, so branch/HEAD/uncommitted
+state could not be inspected — **this may differ from your local checkout; apply the patch, don't overwrite**).
+Audit environment: Node 22.22, no network (npm install produced empty package stubs), no PostgreSQL, no
+Chromium, no OpenAI key.
+
+## 1. Verified working (executed here)
+- `node --check` on all source and test files.
+- Pure test suites: validation, llm, plus the new grounding / jobAnalysis / fit suites — 70/70 pass (see command below).
+- Model `gpt-5.6-luna` and pricing ($0.20 / $1.20 per 1M tokens) corroborated by several third-party pricing pages
+  that cite OpenAI's pricing page; OpenAI's own page was not opened.
+
+## 2. Implemented but NOT verified here
+- Express routes, auth, application CRUD, ownership checks (code reads correctly; DB-backed tests could not run).
+- Prisma migrations (5 present) applying to real Postgres; `prisma validate/generate`.
+- Inngest report job, Playwright PDF rendering, file-serving route.
+- OpenAI Responses API calls (`REQUEST_OPTIONS` second-argument usage not exercised against the real SDK).
+- `auth.test.js` could not run only because `jsonwebtoken` is not installed in the sandbox.
+
+## 3. Broken / incomplete (found by reading the code)
+1. **Committed secrets**: a Postgres password and a JWT secret were hard-coded in `test/*.js`. Treat both as
+   exposed (they are in public git history) — rotate them if they were ever real.
+2. **Tests defaulted to the dev database** (`jobhunt_db`) while creating/deleting rows.
+3. Prisma `datasource` had no `url` (breaks `prisma migrate`/`validate` on Prisma 5) — fixed, unverified.
+4. Port inconsistency: server default and `inngest:dev` used 3001 while `.env.example` and the frontend default used 5000. Standardized on 5000 (the port the project is actually run on).
+5. "Same bullet count" was only a prompt request; a test fixture returned 2 bullets for 1 input and passed.
+6. Prompt-injection: job description concatenated into the prompt unfenced; no request timeout.
+7. `POST /report`: after resetting a FAILED report to PENDING, a failing `inngest.send` leaves it PENDING forever
+   (no timeout/recovery). A DONE report is never regenerated when a newer tailoring exists (stale PDF).
+8. Inngest function's catch marks the report FAILED on any thrown error, possibly before retries are exhausted.
+9. No rate limiting, no pagination, wildcard CORS (acceptable for bearer-token auth, but undocumented), 7-day JWT with no revocation.
+10. README stated migrations were missing (they exist) and the status header is stale.
+11. Product gap: no stored CV/profile (bullets are sent per request), so evidence-based tailoring and fit analysis
+    cannot yet use "the user's actual CV". Frontend is a single applications page; no detail/analysis/interview views.
+
+## 4. Blocked by environment
+Real Postgres tests, Prisma CLI, frontend `npm run build`, Chromium PDF, real LLM call, eslint (none configured).
+
+## 5. Changes made in this pass (all additive or corrective; no schema/billing change)
+See README "AI safeguards". Files: `src/{grounding,promptSafety,jobAnalysis,fit}.js` (new), `src/llm.js`,
+`src/app.js` (adds `grounding` field to `/tailor` response), `prisma/schema.prisma` (datasource url only),
+`.env.example` ×2, `frontend/src/api.js` (default port), tests (3 new suites, llm additions, credential removal).
+Cost accounting is unchanged (`computeCostUsd`).
+
+## 6. Prioritized next steps
+1. Rotate/purge exposed secrets; run migrations + DB-backed tests on a machine with Postgres.
+2. Add `Profile` model (CV text/bullets/skills) + migration → route `POST /applications/:id/analyze` using
+   `analyzeJobDescription` + `assessFit`, persisting results (needs a schema change: decide storage first).
+3. Fix report robustness (#7, #8): send-failure rollback, PENDING timeout, regenerate when tailoring is newer.
+4. Rate limiting on AI routes; per-user daily cost cap from `TailoredResume.costUsd`.
+5. Frontend: application detail, analysis/gap view, tailored-CV review with grounding badges, report status.
+6. Interview prep, only after 2–5.
